==Old English==

===Etymology===
Origin {{unk|ang|obscure}}. Likely a merger of {{cog|ang|cringan}} and {{m|ang|*crenġan}}, {{m|ang|*crenċġan}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*kringaną}} and {{m|gem-pro|*krangijaną}} respectively. Compare {{cog|ofs|krenza}}, {{m|ofs|krinza|t=to harm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ang|/ˈkrind͡ʒɑn/}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=crinċġan}}

# to [[fall]], [[yield]]
# to fall or die in battle

